name="Chainbound Reavers hand flamer" hidden="false" targetId="bb67-e09c-14a9-5c74" type="profile"/><infoLink id="5924-f8e1-ad12-5b49" name="Chainbound Reavers chainaxe" hidden="false" targetId="d56b-0c27-37aa-5050" type="profile"/></infoLinks></selectionEntry></selectionEntries></selectionEntryGroup><selectionEntryGroup id="b611-a558-c942-5a31" name="Optional hand flamer slot 2" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" defaultSelectionEntryId="5893-5895-08e7-5aad"><constraints><constraint id="15f4-79da-5fdd-5fa0" type="min" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/><constraint id="5228-5bfd-49e5-5dc9" type="max" field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/></constraints><selectionEntries><selectionEntry id="ee8f-d6f9-83a9-5e51" name="1 Reaver — autopistol and chainaxe" hidden="false" collective="false" type="upgrade" import="true"><infoLinks><infoLink id="4139-c888-deb4-59a0" name="Chainbound Reavers autopistol" hidden="false" targetId="1515-8c32-0131-5eed" type="profile"/><infoLink id="24b2-cfd9-5edb-5418" name="Chainbound Reavers chainaxe" hidden="false" targetId="d56b-0c27-37aa-5050" type="profile"/></infoLinks></selectionEntry><selectionEntry id="5893-5895-08e7-5aad" name="1 Reaver — hand flamer and chainaxe" hidden="false" collective="false" type="upgrade" import="true"><infoLinks><infoLink id="a02c-1bfc-3868-5a70" name="Chainbound Reavers hand flamer" hidden="false" targetId="bb67-e09c-14a9-5c74" type="profile"/><infoLink id="34a6-25cd-5e16-5da6" name="Chainbound Reavers chainaxe" hidden="false" targetId="d56b-0c27-37aa-5050" type="profile"/></infoLinks></selectionEntry></selectionEntries></selectionEntryGroup></selectionEntryGroups></selectionEntry></selectionEntries></selectionEntryGroup></selectionEntryGroups></selectionEntry></selectionEntries><sharedRules><rule id="2c4e-2b7d-53e1-5d0d" name="Infernal Serum" hidden="false"><description>Each living fully inducted INFERNAL WARRIORS ASTARTES receives +1 starting/max W, Feel No Pain 5+, and heals 1 lost W at the start of its controller’s turn; no revival. Excludes uninducted Scouts, mortals, vehicles, Dreadnoughts, Daemon Engines and daemon allies. Current displayed unit W includes the +1 where eligible.</description></rule><rule id="e0f2-fa24-c84e-59af" name="Disciplined Brutality" hidden="false"><description>At start of Command phase mark a Directed Objective enemy visible to friendly OFFICER or within 12" of VOXMASTER. Once per phase when friendly INFERNAL WARRIORS ASTARTES attacks it in melee and another friendly ASTARTES is within 9" of that enemy, re-roll one Hit and one Wound (subject to normal die re-roll restrictions).</description></rule><rule id="1ed1-86a9-2d02-5af3" name="Warp-Aggravated Pain" hidden="false"><description>Command phase, ordinary ASTARTES within 12" of a non-exempt Psyker or Daemon: D6 3+ pass, 1–2 suffers -1 ranged Hit until next Command phase. Friendly allied Khorne daemons are exempt triggers. Lost Cohort uses separate control.</description></rule><rule id="8da3-eead-cabf-56ea" name="Rare Psychic-Induced Psychosis" hidden="false"><description>At most once per battle round if an enemy Psyker uses a psychic ability/attack within 12" of ordinary ASTARTES, nearest eligible unit rolls 2D6. On 3 or less it prioritizes triggering Psyker where legal; until next friendly Command phase or Psyker destroyed.</description></rule><rule id="3bff-1efe-c60b-511f" name="Lost Cohort — Control" hidden="false"><description>Maximum 2 Lost Cohort units combined. Each starts with its own qualifying attached Chaplain, in addition to 5–10 afflicted warriors. Each afflicted adds +1 Attack on ONE eligible melee profile only. If Chaplain dies, D6 4+ Control Test each Command phase unless supervised by qualifying friendly Chaplain (including allied equivalent) within 12". On failure Aggressive Pursuit: legally move/target/charge nearest enemy; OC retained; cannot start new voluntary mission actions.</description></rule><rule id="88db-cb52-d552-50e7" name="11th-Edition Homebrew Muster" hidden="false"><description>At 1,000 points use up to 2 Detachment Points and 2 Enhancements; at 2,000 points use up to 3 DP and 4 Enhancements. Named characters cannot take normal Enhancements. Detachments: War Hounds’ Legacy costs 2 DP; Crimson Onslaught, Iron Reavers and Breach and Ruin each cost 1 DP. This separate system requires consent, and printed points are provisional. New Recruit default DP budget is 3; set it to 2 for 1,000pt games.</description></rule><rule id="3ecd-6609-5f42-5166" name="Khorne Ally Allowance" hidden="false"><description>Optional KHORNE DAEMON ally allowance up to 25% of agreed army points. Daemon allies do not receive Infernal Serum, Disciplined Brutality, or Infernal Warriors detachment effects. This percentage and separate army coalition legality currently require manual checking.</description></rule><rule id="2ebc-af04-8c25-5029" name="Unified Forces — Coalition (Homebrew)" hidden="false"><description>The permanent Unified Forces cooperation doctrine of the Infernal Warriors, Frozen Cogs, and Abandoned Dead applies in appropriate 2v2 coalition battles, not only Gaul. The partners remain separate playable armies; outside players must consent. Allied codices will have their own data files when authored.</description></rule><rule id="03fea306-e073-5356" name="Legion Teleportarium" hidden="false"><description>All Infernal Warriors TERMINATOR Infantry units and eligible Terminator-armoured Leaders gain Deep Strike at no additional points. This does not grant first-battle-round arrival; respect mission Reserves timing and placement rules.</description></rule><rule id="595a068d-663b-51e6" name="Pilot Resilience" hidden="false"><description>Eligible Contemptor, Leviathan, Deredeo and Helbrute pilots: once per battle round, immediately after failing a saving throw against a Damage 1 attack, re-roll that saving throw. This protects the surviving pilot; the hull does not regenerate.</description></rule><rule id="4bbaac30-6adb-5c5f" name="Cohort Insertion" hidden="false"><description>Each of up to TWO Lost Cohort formations may arrive independently using Deep Strike in the Reinforcements step of YOUR first Movement phase, even where the normal first-round arrival prohibition would apply. The required paid attached Chaplain arrives with it. This does not waive Reserves caps, more-than-8-inch enemy exclusion, coherency, legal 9+ charge roll after standard placement, or mission timing other than the turn-one exception. An embarked transport does not inherit the exception.</description></rule><rule id="dcda18a8-c302-54e3" name="Vox-Directed Advance" hidden="false"><description>Once per battle round, one friendly INFERNAL WARRIORS ASTARTES INFANTRY unit that started the turn on the battlefield can re-roll its Advance roll, keeping the new result. Does not confer Advance-and-Charge/Shoot or affect arrivals from Reserves that turn.</description></rule><rule id="f4c7de0f-8a1a-503b" name="Mechanised Vanguard" hidden="false"><description>After both armies deploy, choose up to ONE friendly non-AIRCRAFT INFERNAL WARRIORS TRANSPORT with INFANTRY embarked for each FULL 1,000 points of battle limit (maximum TWO). Each may make one Normal Move of up to 3 inches, ending outside enemy deployment zone and more than 9 inches from enemy models, where mission permits. No new arrival or charge privilege.</description></rule><rule id="52fee7ba-5ef8-5737" name="Khorne Daemon Allies" hidden="false"><description>Only the five listed Khorne daemonic allied profiles are supported in this faction catalogue. Up to 25% of the ARMY POINTS limit may be Khorne Daemons, as a PROVISIONAL homebrew allowance. They do not benefit from Infernal Serum, Disciplined Brutality or chapter detachments. Verify allowance manually.</description></rule><rule id="f45d38e4-bfe7-5602" name="Named Character Enhancement Lock" hidden="false"><description>All unique named Infernal Warriors characters are EPIC HERO-equivalent for mustering: they may not receive ordinary Character Enhancements. Their own abilities and Leader status are unaffected.</description></rule><rule id="8e4d6e8b-1aaf-5e67" name="Leader Attachment Eligibility" hidden="false"><description>Leaders join only their codex-listed compatible bodyguards. Normally one Leader, with an additional Support only if explicitly permitted. Lost Cohort must begin with its OWN paid qualifying Chaplain; Captains, apothecaries and Voxmasters do NOT substitute. Check actual roster pairings manually where the data editor does not enforce them.</description></rule><rule id="2adf0699-3369-4040-8ff5-7139af7a314e" name="Leader Eligibility — Balan Bannon" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Infernal Legionaries, Chosen Veterans, Infernal Berzerkers, Infernal Butchers. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="c77b26be-741b-4fe5-b0d4-e29ef6ba921f" name="Leader Eligibility — Varroth" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Ashen Chain Terminators, Cataphractii Terminator Veterans, Tartaros Terminator Veterans. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="166c4edd-babf-43d8-9994-fc42de50078a" name="Leader Eligibility — Rhazek Thorne" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Infernal Legionaries, Despoiler Cadre, Chosen Veterans. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="3b8acffc-fae8-4570-8d78-588cf0ae55fd" name="Leader Eligibility — Kordas Vrenn" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Void Breachers, Infernal Legionaries, Chosen Veterans. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="c9b3d8d9-10a5-4926-860a-7d2244abeaae" name="Leader Eligibility — Dravik Sorn" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Void Breachers, Despoiler Cadre, Chosen Veterans. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="c06013a6-8247-4f30-9774-083fc0dc2c5b" name="Leader Eligibility — Varkhul Renn" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Infernal Legionaries, Recon Veterans, Tactical Support Cadre. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="b8c51b72-a483-4ca7-a791-dab2d35e7899" name="Leader Eligibility — Torgath Keld" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Infernal Legionaries, Heavy Support Cadre, Chosen Veterans. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="73000c65-26b5-4db4-89b7-9988e2697553" name="Leader Eligibility — Malthor Ghor" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Recon Veterans, Infernal Legionaries, Despoiler Cadre. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="9729d83d-df2f-4bf8-8c64-77eebca9f050" name="Leader Eligibility — Azrakh Drenn" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Assault Jump Cadre, Raptor Strike Cadre. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="81dfddc2-6d2d-4e6b-b2d4-5ab951b42cd9" name="Leader Eligibility — Velkan Rusk" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Heavy Support Cadre, Tactical Support Cadre, Infernal Legionaries. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="9444299f-ab76-4830-b20a-4001f0a7b200" name="Leader Eligibility — Varek Thul" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Tenth Company Scouts, Recon Veterans, Infernal Legionaries. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="a2af1900-a7c2-40a8-9d3a-51194f9fdcaf" name="Leader Eligibility — Orvath Krail" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Infernal Legionaries, Chosen Veterans. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="370778a4-869f-410d-9522-712a892ea58f" name="Leader Eligibility — Istran Valcor" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Infernal Legionaries, Chosen Veterans, Infernal Berzerkers. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="f864090c-27e3-4b65-a7eb-da20a74adda7" name="Leader Eligibility — Tervan Khol" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Infernal Berzerkers, Infernal Butchers, Chosen Veterans. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="c7219d8a-a874-4fc3-9fe3-a8734baf2a07" name="Leader Eligibility — Mordren Vhal" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Infernal Legionaries, Chosen Veterans. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="52027dfe-1c05-4d1a-98a1-14d1c0dd70c5" name="Leader Eligibility — Kessel Rane" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Infernal Legionaries, Tactical Support Cadre, Heavy Support Cadre. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="a563efbe-c0a7-4595-aa2f-28f9d8687313" name="Leader Eligibility — Rhazdan Krell" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Chosen Veterans, Infernal Butchers, Despoiler Cadre. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="da1962f0-0e1d-44cd-8167-4b80368d52ac" name="Leader Eligibility — Zecer Varthis" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Ashen Chain Terminators, Cataphractii Terminator Veterans. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="4850b1e3-fe55-4ea8-9e74-f9e80e4b9d74" name="Leader Eligibility — Karnus Vehl" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Ashen Chain Terminators. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="bef1208b-b66f-427c-b3a8-bf042196700c" name="Leader Eligibility — Infernal Chaplain" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Infernal Legionaries, Infernal Berzerkers, Despoiler Cadre, Void Breachers. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="3cb31661-628b-4f26-9cef-5413dec46e6b" name="Leader Eligibility — Infernal Terminator Chaplain" hidden="false"><description>This Leader can join: Ashen Chain Terminators, Cataphractii Terminator Veterans, Tartaros Terminator Veterans. Choose a particular bodyguard unit during Declare Battle Formations; normal limits apply. If the New Recruit native Leader association control appears, use that to identify the specific unit. The in-catalogue bodyguard-type choice remains an explicit fallback and does not create an extra squad.</description></rule><rule id="b0a7-02c8-f70c-54d4" name="Mortal War-Host and Blood Rites" hidden="false"><description>Bloodmarked Thralls and Chainbound Reavers are INFERNAL WARRIORS mortal units; they never count toward inducted Astartes strength and never receive Infernal Serum, +1 W, FNP 5+, regeneration or other ASTARTES-only effects. Pexi 270th remains organized renegade Guard, Thralls remain Khorne cultists/labourers, and Reavers are respected mortal assault troops. Bloodletter Invocation is once per battle PER ARMY, by one eligible non-Battle-shocked Thralls unit on the battlefield, selecting only a purchased BLOODLETTERS unit already in legal Reserves. Bloodletters count against the permitted Khorne Daemon allies (maximum 25% of agreed army points); this is no free summoning, no Reserve cap/timing waiver, and no permission to call non-Khorne or other Daemon models.</description></rule></sharedRules><sharedProfiles><profile id="883a-5ac2-abab-5817" name="Boltgun" hidden="false" typeId="a4f5-4674-06d7-5496" typeName="Weapon"><characteristics><characteristic name="Range" typeId="8aa7-21a6-b6c1-50e6">24"</characteristic><characteristic name="A" typeId="1df3-e803-7074-57ce">2</characteristic><characteristic name="BS/WS" typeId="a16c-0b6c-2681-5f8f">3+</characteristic><characteristic name="S" typeId="846d-1dce-303c-5c75">4</characteristic><characteristic name="AP" typeId="91f2-51a2-9429-5a60">0</characteristic><characteristic name="D" typeId="14cd-2ade-2ccc-5c11">1</characteristic><characteristic name="Traits" typeId="0f05-4353-204c-511f">Rapid Fire 1</characteristic></characteristics></profile><profile id="f413-b65b-eb0c-5cdc" name="Bolt rifle" hidden="false" typeId="a4f5-4674-06d7-5496" typeName="Weapon"><characteristics><characteristic name="Range" typeId="8aa7-21a6-b6c1-50e6">30"</characteristic><characteristic name="A" typeId="1df3-e803-7074-57ce">2</characteristic><characteristic name="BS/WS" typeId="a16c-0b6c-2681-5f8f">3+</characteristic><characteristic name="S" typeId="846d-1dce-303c-5c75">4</characteristic><characteristic name="AP" typeId="91f2-51a2-9429-5a60">-1</characteristic><characteristic name="D" typeId="14cd-2ade-2ccc-5c11">1</characteristic><characteristic name="Traits" typeId="0f05-4353-204c-511f">Assault</characteristic></characteristics></profile><profile id="dff3-0c25-ce32-57a1" name="Scoped bolt rifle" hidden="false" typeId="a4f5-4674-06d7-5496" typeName="Weapon"><characte